OL,3,ABritish chess prodigy, 11, becomes
OL,4,Ayoungest woman grandmaster
OL,5,
OL,6,FA British child chess prodigy has
OL,7,Fbecome the youngest player in history
OL,8,Fto earn the woman grandmaster (WGM)
OL,9,Ftitle.
OL,11,FBodhana Sivanandan, 11, from north-west
OL,12,FLondon, secured her third and final WGM
OL,13,Fnorm - a certified title-level
OL,14,Fperformance - while representing
OL,15,FEngland at the 46th Chess Olympiad in
OL,16,FSamarkand, Uzbekistan, the
OL,17,FInternational Chess Federation (FIDE)
OL,18,Fconfirmed.
OL,20,FSpeaking to FIDE, Sivanandan said she
OL,21,Fwas happy about the achievement but
OL,22,Fwanted to "keep making history".
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
